WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:01.470
Fear not.

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:05.720
If you trust in the possibilities
within and try with all your might,

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.680
the path will show itself to you!

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:10.760
No... it's too late for that.
It's selfish.

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:14.180
Please forgive me.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:19.840
I wanted to spend more...
much more...

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.630
Father!

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:34.180
Father...? Did I... just now...

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:37.220
My own...

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.300
To my only desire...

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:56.680
The beast of possibility...

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:00.970
The symbol of hope... Father...

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:07.720
I'm sorry, Mom. I must...

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.380
...go!

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:01.260
It is now 23:40 Greenwich Mean Time.

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:06.130
One world is about to end,
and a new one is about to be born.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.880
The Earth Federation government
is about to host a ceremony

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:11.800
at the Prime Minister's
residence, "Laplace",

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:14.340
to usher in the birth of
the new calendar era.

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:17.050
Mankind has set foot into a new era,

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:18.970
in which we shall build
for ourselves worlds to live in,

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:20.430
beyond Mother Earth.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:26.510
Tonight, we shall become
witnesses to history.

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:29.260
Let us come together in
this joyous moment

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:34.630
and give thanks to the past,
the Anno Domini era.

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:41.300
Also, let us welcome in the dawn of the
Universal Century with smiling faces.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:46.300
Goodbye, Anno Domini.
Hello, Universal Century!

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:52.470
Greetings, citizens of Earth and space.

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:58.510
I am the Prime Minister of the
Earth Federation, Ricardo Marcenas.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.970
In a few moments,
the Anno Domini era will come to an end.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:05.220
...Presidents and Prime Ministers spoke

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.470
only to the citizens
of their respective countries.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:11.010
These countries were composed
of citizenries and territories,

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:16.880
designed in the solitary interest
of protecting their own security.

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:20.260
Yet, as we've now realized
humanity's long-awaited dream

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.630
of a unified world government,

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:24.630
we can look back on the
antiquated nation-state system

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:27.300
and see the problems
that came with it.

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:31.090
Just as no man is an
island unto himself,

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:35.760
a nation is incapable of functioning
in a solitary vacuum.

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:38.380
In regards to the threats to
the planet as a whole,

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:43.470
the nations of old were incapable
of offering effective solutions.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:49.260
Rhetoric and sitting idly by
are no longer options. We must...

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:53.130
How is it?

00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:57.380
We'll go ahead as planned.

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:01.880
This might cause more chaos
than we've ever known.

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:07.380
It's almost been one hundred
years since then.

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:12.050
As it stands, the Earth Sphere
is approaching a dead end.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:16.930
Those who will correct the flaws
of the Universal Century

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:19.340
are beginning to emerge.

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:25.130
I pray the one who can be entrusted to
carry Laplace's Box is among them.

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:27.510
Yes, sir.

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:30.380
Cardeas...

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:35.720
Do you forgive me?

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:43.970
This may lead to the end of a world.

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:47.840
Who could forgive you besides me?

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:08.470
(DEPARTURE 0096)

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:15.800
Disperse Minovsky Particles
at combat density, now!

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:19.430
Enemy ship, appears to be Clop class...
Thermal energy detected!

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:20.550
Evasive maneuvers!

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:38.510
What's taking so long
with the bulkheads?!

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:41.590
Intense heat sources emitted
from enemy ship.

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:44.090
Appears to be two mobile suits...

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:46.550
No, three! Approaching
at high speed!

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:47.800
Send Marida out.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:51.380
Ignore the mothership.
The Garencieres can shake it off.

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:52.430
Roger that.

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:00.380
Target acquired.

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:04.010
There's a high-speed Jegan.
Possibly a special forces version.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:06.180
That means this isn't a chance encounter.

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:08.880
Ten minutes to the debris cluster.

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:10.510
Wrap things up and get back here.

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:12.720
Roger that, Master.

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:14.880
Stop calling me that.

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:20.970
Marida Cruz. Launching in Kshatriya!

00:08:39.970 --> 00:08:41.260
I won't let you follow our ship.

00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:43.550
Funnels!

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:18.630
Damn Sleeves!

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:25.840
Mission complete. Returning to ship.

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:44.760
Thus, it was the Battle of A Baoa Qu

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:47.220
which brought an end
to the One Year War,

00:10:47.260 --> 00:10:49.090
started by the Principality of Zeon

00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:51.590
in the name of independence
for the space emigrants.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:56.010
At the end of the war, over
half of humanity was dead.

00:10:56.590 --> 00:11:02.260
This happened seventeen years ago,
the year before you all were born.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.300
Even after the war,

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:08.180
groups claiming to be the remnants
of Zeon started wars of their own.

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:13.180
They claim to desire autonomy for
the Spacenoids, but at their heart

00:11:13.220 --> 00:11:16.720
you will still find the same ideas of the
inherent superiority of the chosen elite

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:19.300
found in the philosophy
of Gihren Zabi.

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:23.050
The concept of Zeonism proposed
by Zeon Deikun, the so-called

00:11:23.090 --> 00:11:27.840
"Newtype" ideology, was a
dangerous belief that ultimately

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:30.510
produced rebellious elements
such as these.

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:33.470
You there!

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:39.050
Don't blow off studying history because
you think it won't help get you a job!

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:43.260
Anaheim won't even hire you
for a factory worker position,

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:45.130
if you're not capable of
passing senior high.

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:49.340
Don't believe everything you hear about
that 100% job placement rate- -

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:51.720
Mr. Bancroft, it's the shuttle again...

00:11:58.970 --> 00:12:01.720
It's seriously time to upgrade
our shuttles.

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:03.550
The chairman's just stingy.

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:06.130
He thinks that the decommissioned
Anaheim ones are fine.

00:12:06.180 --> 00:12:08.590
So we're staying here tonight?

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:09.970
I didn't bring a change of clothes.

00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:11.380
Neither did I.

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:14.760
Which means we won't get to go on the
field trip to see the Snail tomorrow.

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:20.340
What?! I don't want to spend two days here
listening to Bancroft's "special" lectures!

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:24.470
I could teach all the way to
Char's Rebellion in two minutes.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.050
Right, Banagher?

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:32.220
Wow, look at that! It's a Zaku!

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:34.720
Damn it, Bancroft.

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:37.840
Why didn't you tell us there was
something this cool here?

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:39.800
What's that? Is it something cool?

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:42.880
It's the granddaddy
of all mobile suits!

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:43.840
Oh...?

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:46.340
Hey, wait up. Let's check it out.

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:47.510
Don't care.

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:50.630
The wars ended a long time ago.
We don't need those things anymore.

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:52.880
I'm pretty sure you aren't
allowed to take pictures.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:56.050
You guys have no sense
of adventure, seriously.

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:06.220
Say, Banagher,

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:10.130
you know sometimes you look like
you're staring out into the distance.

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:12.340
- Yeah?
- Yeah. You just did it back there.

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:15.840
I'm not really looking at anything
in particular when I do that...

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:16.800
Huh?

00:13:18.010 --> 00:13:21.050
I think I'm just wondering where...

00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:23.430
Where your father is?

00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:25.010
No, where I am.

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:26.050
Oh, sorry.

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:30.840
Like whatever I'm doing...
I'm not really there, you know?

00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:36.430
I have the same feeling.
Like something's just off, right?

00:13:36.470 --> 00:13:37.470
Yeah...

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:42.800
I wonder if it's gonna keep
getting stronger and stronger.

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:45.630
I think the only ones who don't feel it

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:49.680
are the few who get to
live their lives how they want to.

00:13:56.510 --> 00:13:58.180
Hey, are you listening to me?

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:04.720
A mobile suit...

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:22.220
Keep the speed going.

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:23.180
Y-Yes, sir.

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:29.550
Fly like you're going straight
into that debris field.

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:38.180
Keep going.

00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:41.880
Sir!

00:14:43.180 --> 00:14:44.680
Breakdown 0-6-0.

00:14:55.180 --> 00:14:56.760
Impressive.

00:14:56.800 --> 00:14:57.930
Th-Thank you.

00:14:57.970 --> 00:14:59.260
I'm talking about the machine.

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:00.630
Yes, sir.

00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:01.680
At ease.

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:13.590
We're going back, Gael.

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:15.800
I'm sorry, sir.

00:15:15.840 --> 00:15:17.010
What's wrong?

00:15:17.050 --> 00:15:18.340
It appears there were still people

00:15:18.380 --> 00:15:21.180
at the Anaheim Electronics
Industrial College training facility.

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:23.760
I thought we checked
the class schedule...

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:26.630
It seems the transit
shuttle broke down.

00:15:26.680 --> 00:15:30.930
I see... Well, even if
someone noticed it,

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:33.970
it couldn't have been more
than a momentary glimpse.

00:15:39.630 --> 00:15:43.050
I was able to get hold of
a staff officer on Luna II.

00:15:43.090 --> 00:15:48.090
It's true, a Londo Bell ship
ran into some Sleeves.

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:51.090
So there was a leak...
Was there a battle?

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:54.840
Yes. Not only did they lose three mobile
suits, but they let them get away.

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:56.090
Anything else?

00:15:56.130 --> 00:15:59.800
I tried Londenion, but their commander
is a very tight-lipped person.

00:15:59.840 --> 00:16:01.970
Bright Noa, is it?

00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:03.510
Try the supply fleets, then.

00:16:03.550 --> 00:16:05.090
You'll be able to figure out
how the fleet itself is moving.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:06.510
Certainly.

00:16:06.550 --> 00:16:08.590
Everyone, listen up.

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:12.760
All operational testing of the
RX-0 is now finished.

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:16.180
We are to immediately
delete the testing OS.

00:16:16.220 --> 00:16:19.930
Seal the NT-D, and boot
up the La+ Program.

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:48.300
"Forgive", huh?

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:13.090
Roger that. Entering gate #5.

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:16.430
What is this "Laplace's Box" thing?

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:18.680
If they really have it,
we'll bring it back home.

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:20.590
If it's a trap, we'll fight our way out.

00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:49.970
Man, this weightlessness is getting to me.

00:18:50.010 --> 00:18:53.260
Lemme skip the Snail field trip.

00:18:53.300 --> 00:18:55.880
It's 'cause you were
partying all night.

00:18:55.930 --> 00:18:58.260
I just don't find looking at the
Construction Unit all that interesting.

00:18:58.300 --> 00:19:01.220
But guys, it's not often people get
to see the inside of that thing.

00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:07.180
Banagher!

00:19:07.220 --> 00:19:08.130
Don't ask, Micott.

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:09.180
Banagher, bathroom?

00:19:09.220 --> 00:19:10.680
I'm going back ahead of you guys!

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:12.180
That looks bad over there.

00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:19.720
I can't die...

00:19:28.880 --> 00:19:30.510
Hey! What're you doing?!

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:31.550
I'm borrowing this.

00:19:31.590 --> 00:19:34.220
Like hell you are! Hey, wait! Hey!

00:19:37.430 --> 00:19:39.340
Ah! Hey!

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:41.680
It's not like being in a vacuum.

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:50.680
Found you, but it's almost
daybreak... This is bad.

00:19:53.840 --> 00:19:56.010
I'm not yet...

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:18.050
Danger. Danger.

00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:25.380
I'll get us through this.

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:39.680
Clench your teeth!

00:20:44.590 --> 00:20:45.510
Danger. Danger.

00:20:54.840 --> 00:20:56.470
Banagher, wake up.

00:20:58.180 --> 00:21:00.220
Banagher, wake up.

00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:19.220
Ow-ow-ow...

00:21:19.260 --> 00:21:20.180
Who are you?!

00:21:20.220 --> 00:21:21.180
What do you think you're doing?!

00:21:21.220 --> 00:21:23.760
Banagher, are you OK? Banagher?

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:25.010
Are you from this colony?

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:30.970
I'm in a hurry. Can you give me a lift
to the Colony Builder's entrance?

00:21:31.760 --> 00:21:33.300
To the Snail?

00:21:33.340 --> 00:21:34.930
Will this thing still work?

00:21:34.970 --> 00:21:37.340
It's out of gas. The battery's dead too.

00:21:37.380 --> 00:21:39.090
I'm running out of time! Please!

00:21:39.930 --> 00:21:42.340
There's someone I absolutely
must speak with.

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:45.340
If we don't hurry, something will happen
that can never be undone.

00:21:45.380 --> 00:21:48.130
But we can still prevent it if
we act fast. So please...

00:21:48.180 --> 00:21:50.430
Prevent it? Prevent what?

00:21:50.470 --> 00:21:51.430
War.

00:21:57.470 --> 00:21:58.510
Hold on!

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:05.550
You can't do this alone.

00:23:38.260 --> 00:23:43.340
Next time, on Mobile Suit Gundam Unicorn
FIRST BLOOD,

00:23:45.010 --> 00:23:48.380
awaken the Newtype that lies within you.
